      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# PART 3 - Render video with LTX 2.5\n\nPick the run whose cards you approved in Part 2.\n\n**RENDER SEGMENTS** builds a complete LTX 2.5 first/last-frame graph for each unfinished segment. To keep memory bounded, one execution renders `segments_per_queue` clips (default 4). Every clip is saved immediately under the run, and completed clips are skipped next time.\n\nQueue repeatedly until the status panel reports that all clips are present, or set ComfyUI's Queue batch count to the number of remaining batches shown in the report. Lower `segments_per_queue` if memory is tight.\n\n**THE FEED** lists every segment, timecode, frame count, card pair, seed, prompt, and render status. LTX frame counts use the required `8k + 1` layout, so the stitcher trims each clip to the exact song segment.\n\n`end_guide_strength` defaults to 0.7, matching the official first/last-frame setup. Lower values allow more motion but can weaken the match to the ending card; higher values pull harder toward it.\n\nTo rerender selected segments, delete their `clips/clip_NNN.mp4` files and queue again. Turning `resume` off rerenders the full selected range in one execution and can require much more memory.\n\nOutputs stay inside the run: `clips/`, `segments/`, and `final_music_video.mp4`. The final file is complete once every segment clip is present."
      ],
      "title": "READ ME",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
